{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "scriptId": "pl-04-quantity-rates-item-equivalences",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Quantity Rates and Item Equivalences",
    "description": "Handle ‘x for ₹y’, dozens, C.P. of one quantity equals S.P. of another, and profit equal to the price of some units.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use common batches instead of awkward unit decimals. Move from 'x for ₹y' rates to C.P./S.P. quantity equivalences, gain/loss equal to some units, items-per-rupee targets and free-item discounts, always preserving what each count means.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 28,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 12, Profit and Loss. Approved scope: Teach quantity-price forms without converting every item separately. Use a common batch or L.C.M. for statements such as bought 6 for ₹10 and sold 4 for ₹6. Cover C.P. of m articles = S.P. of n articles, gain/loss equal to S.P. or C.P. of some units, how many items per rupee must be bought or sold for a target gain, and free-item offers as an effective discount. Keep the unit meaning visible so learners do not invert buying and selling rates. End with a capstone combining a quantity equivalence with a target percentage."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn quantity rates and item equivalences.\n\nA vendor buys 6 bananas for ₹10 and sells 4 for ₹6. The item counts are different, so comparing ₹10 and ₹6 directly tells us nothing. A common batch makes the deal visible.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Rates such as ‘6 bananas for ₹10’ are easiest when you compare a common batch. You do not need awkward per-banana decimals.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Bought 6 for ₹10 and sold 4 for ₹6.\nUse 12 bananas.\nC.P. = 2 × 10 = ₹20.\nS.P. = 3 × 6 = ₹18.\nLoss = 10%.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
